gaC4(){return"Everything here is money, not percentages, and that is deliberate.\n\nEvery figure replays your REAL buys and sells \u2014 the same amounts, on the same days \u2014 into each alternative. So the gap between two rows is an actual amount you can act on.\n\nWhy not percentages? A percentage has to be a percentage OF something, and the honest denominator here is every purchase you have ever made. Sell a holding and buy it back and the same money is counted twice, so the percentage shrinks the more you trade even when your profit is identical. The amount does not move.\n\nDividends count as cash on both sides: yours, and each target's own payouts. Neither side reinvests them.\n\nFor an annual rate, see the Personal IRR card above \u2014 that is the one figure here that is per year."},
