gaKp(){return"Historical VaR reflects your actual portfolio's past volatility \u2014 not a theoretical model. Past volatility does not guarantee future losses."},
gaKq(){return'Answers: "On a bad day/week, how much could I lose?"\n\nMethod: Historical simulation \u2014 uses your actual past portfolio returns to estimate the loss you could expect on your worst days. No assumptions about return distributions.\n\n\u26a0 Weekly VaR is scaled from your daily VaR, adjusted for how often you actually open the app. Real markets can have extreme events \u2014 actual losses can occasionally exceed this estimate.\n\nVaR does NOT predict the maximum possible loss.'},
